# Interview Transcript with Raisa

**Q: What information about courses do you think is the most important?**  
A: Of course the overview of what the course is about and also the assessment system, like is it exam-based or project-based.  

---

**Q: Would you find a custom plan for your entire degree useful? Would you use it?**  
A: Yes, of course, I would definitely use it to plan out my study load for each semester.  

---

**Q: If you could redesign UQ's public programs and courses page, would you? How?**  
A: I would make it clearer what courses are available, especially for electives, like providing the full list of optional courses that students can take.  

---

**Q: What do you find is the most annoying feature of the course profile?**  
A: I think it’s already good and quite clear, there’s nothing particularly annoying.  

---

**Q: If you take a dual degree, have you seen your planner? What did you like about it? What didn’t you like about it?**  
A: Usually, in the final semester, the courses are harder, level 3 and above. I think it would be better if the workload was more balanced across the semesters.  

---

**Q: Do you use Allocate+’s timetable? What don’t you like about it? What do you like about it?**  
A: We have to adjust the schedule by ourselves. It can be overwhelming if there are a lot of clashes since it’s hard to visualize what’s happening at which time.  

---

**Q: What UQ website has your favourite UI design? What has your least favourite design?**  
A: I like the UI of Blackboard and UQ’s main website, and I think Allocate is the least favourite one because the UI is plain and old.  

---

**Q: Would you find it useful if our website offered alternative courses to take if the course you were going to take ends up full or for some other reason you can no longer take it?**  
A: Of course, that would be really helpful so I wouldn’t have to search around for alternative courses.  

---

**Q: Do you think being able to plan your entire degree out in a visual timeline will reduce confusion compared to just the current list of courses?**  
A: Yeah, I think having a visual will make it much easier to understand than just looking at a list.  

---

**Q: Have you seen a student talk about your specific degree? Do you think if you did it would make course selection less overwhelming?**  
A: Yeah, it would be very helpful to know about other students’ opinions on some courses or degrees so we won’t feel overwhelmed about what’s coming next.  

---

**Q: Do you think having a space to chat with other students who are doing the same course or have done the same course in the past will help?**  
A: Yeah, because we can learn from other students’ opinions about that course and we can prepare before we get into the course.  
